   "exterior": "half-space even-mode DtN, discretized EXACTLY as follows (two other faithful readings move the per-level values by up to 3.2e-4): for modes n = 0..11, c_n(u) = sum over the outer-boundary facets, sum over the degree-(2k+4) Gauss-Legendre points q of the facet, of w_q |J_q| (r_q / Rb^2) P_2n(z_q / |x_q|) u(x_q), with x_q = (r_q, z_q) the PHYSICAL quadrature point (on the straight P1 facet or on the isoparametric P2 facet) and |J_q| the facet length Jacobian; the bilinear term added to the per-radian stiffness is sum_n kappa Rb (2n+1)(4n+1) c_n(phi) c_n(v), kappa the electrolyte conductivity of the case. Facets are straight for P1; for P2 the outer-arc edge node is the radial projection of the chord midpoint onto rho = Rb (the arc point at the mean polar angle of the two vertices); every other edge node is the straight midpoint. Derivation: phi = sum a_n (Rb/rho)^(2n+1) P_2n(cos th), a_n = (4n+1) int_0^{pi/2} phi P_2n sin th dth (insulating plane z = 0 outside the hemisphere). axi::ElectroProblem's full-sphere map must not be used.",
   "meshes": {
